 ## Background
-Hierarchical Sampling (Inverse CDF Sampling) originates from the NeRF (Neural Radiance Fields) paper by Mildenhall et al. [S2, S5, unofficial]. It was introduced to improve the efficiency of volume rendering by concentrating samples in regions of high density. The method has been widely adopted in subsequent works, including [S1, S4, S7, unofficial]. It is a key component in many modern neural rendering pipelines.
